## 2. Memory Arenas & Polymorphic Memory Resources (`std::pmr`)

Avoid fine-grained heap allocations in hot loops. Use monotonic arena allocators:

```cpp
#include <memory_resource>
#include <vector>
#include <string>

void ProcessFrameBatch() {
    // 64 KB stack-allocated buffer for zero-malloc hot execution
    std::array<std::byte, 64 * 1024> stackBuffer;
    std::pmr::monotonic_buffer_resource pool(
        stackBuffer.data(), 
        stackBuffer.size(), 
        std::pmr::null_memory_resource() // Disallow heap fallback
    );

    // Fast vector allocations inside the arena
    std::pmr::vector<std::pmr::string> messages(&pool);
    messages.reserve(128);

    for (int i = 0; i < 100; ++i) {
        messages.emplace_back("Telemetry payload packet #" + std::to_string(i), &pool);
    }
    // Entire arena is reset at scope exit without individual deallocation overhead
}
```

