## 3. Cache-Friendly Data-Oriented Design (DoD)

### 3.1 Structure of Arrays (SoA) vs Array of Structures (AoS)
Maximize CPU L1/L2 cache hit rate by separating hot and cold fields:

```cpp
#include <vector>
#include <new>

// Cache line aligned structure to avoid false sharing
struct alignas(std::hardware_destructive_interference_size) ParticleSystemSoA {
    std::vector<float> posX;
    std::vector<float> posY;
    std::vector<float> posZ;
    std::vector<float> velX;
    std::vector<float> velY;
    std::vector<float> velZ;
    std::vector<uint32_t> entityIds;

    void UpdatePositions(float dt, size_t count) noexcept {
        // Continuous memory reads yield maximum SIMD auto-vectorization
        for (size_t i = 0; i < count; ++i) {
            posX[i] += velX[i] * dt;
            posY[i] += velY[i] * dt;
            posZ[i] += velZ[i] * dt;
        }
    }
};
```

